Replace `"C:\path\to\your\scripts\myscript.ps1"` with the actual path to your PowerShell script.

3. Now, call this PowerCLI script in your Terraform configuration:

```hcl
provider "powershell" {
  version = "3.0.0"
}

output "script_output" {
  value = jsonencode({
    result = powershell_script.call_script.stdout
  })
}

resource "powershell_script" "call_script" {
  inline = [
    "C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\path\to\your\scripts\call_script.ps1 -input \"Your Input String\"",
  ]
}
```

Replace `"Your Input String"` with the desired input value for your PowerShell script. This method passes the input as a string argument to the PowerCLI script.

