GridFS is a popular solution that splits large files into smaller chunks and stores them as separate documents in a MongoDB collection. This makes it easier to manage and retrieve binary data efficiently. To work with GridFS, you will need to install the `gridfs-stream` package if you're using Node.js or the `gridfs` package if you're using Python.

Here's an example of how to save an image using Node.js:

